  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "A linear system of ODEs has the equilibrium at ${x}^{\u2217}=[-2,\\,4]^{T}.$ The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}.$ After shifting using $u=x-{x}^{\u2217},$ the system becomes ${u}^{\u2032}=Au.$ Which of the following is **guaranteed** to be an eigenvalue of the matrix $A?$",
  "worked_solution": "After shifting a linear system, the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors remain unchanged.\n\nThus, the matrix $A$ in the shifted system has the same eigenvalues as the system's matrix in the original coordinates. These eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ or any expressions that are equal to them.\n\nAmong the given options, the only quantity that is guaranteed to be an eigenvalue of $A$ is ${\\lambda }_{2}.$",
